# Comis Lossless Context DAG real-LLM regression driver — operator config TEMPLATE.
# Copy to scripts/lcd-regression.env and fill in the values you need, then export
# them before running the env-gated driver:
#
#   set -a; . scripts/lcd-regression.env; set +a
#   pnpm vitest run packages/agent/src/context-engine/real-llm-regression.bench.test.ts
#
# scripts/lcd-regression.env is git-ignored — NEVER commit real keys. The driver
# reads these vars via process.env at the .test.ts boundary and forwards the key to
# pi-ai's typed `apiKey` option; nothing is stored, logged, or echoed.

# ── Gate ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The driver (real-llm-regression.bench.test.ts) is SKIPPED entirely unless this is
# set. Absent → describe.skipIf skips the suite → no provider call, no network, no
# cost (this is the state under the default `pnpm test` / `pnpm validate`).
COMIS_LCD_REGRESSION=1

# ── Answer LLM (REQUIRED to run the provider-backed probes) ──────────────────────
# The model the driver drives a real completion against in the tool-free baseline
# probe. Absent any of the three → the probes self-skip (it.skipIf). Pin a DATED
# snapshot for reproducibility.
#COMIS_LCD_ANSWER_PROVIDER=anthropic
#COMIS_LCD_ANSWER_MODEL=<answer-model-id>
#COMIS_LCD_ANSWER_API_KEY=<answer-api-key>

# ── Cost bound (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Caps the number of real provider calls the suite makes when enabled. Set to 0 for
# a record-only ($0) run: the structural stream:context / assembledShape assertions
# still execute, but no live LLM call is made. Absent → the default probe count.
#COMIS_LCD_LIMIT=1
